@startuml
title JOB-02 - daily00:30 fixed source set and late adjustments (REVIEW)
autonumber
participant "Daily runner / authorized admin" as W
participant "Report period / run" as P
participant "Committed financial history" as L
participant "Source memberships / contributions" as C
participant "Daily summary" as S
participant "Optional CSV export" as E
W -> P : claim original day / missing backlog day
W -> P : get or durably record FIRST cutoff before source work
P --> W : original cutoff, unchanged on all retries
alt first durable source freeze absent
 W -> L : one consistent selection for recordedAt local day\nusing original cutoff
 L --> W : committed qualifying sources
 W -> C : persist fixed source members / immutable amounts
 W -> P : persist snapshot identity / SNAPSHOTTED with members
else retry existing fixed period
 P --> W : reuse SAME cutoff / membership
end
W -> C : claim each source globally once as BASE
W -> S : aggregate only persisted contributions
W -> P : reconcile then publish FINALIZED
... committed old-day source discovered after finalization ...
W -> L : detect eligible unrepresented source
W -> C : unique source => ADJUSTMENT in later period\nretain original local day
W -> S : include once in later period, never mutate finalized original
W -> E : export immutable finalized version if requested
alt export fails
 E --> W : retry export only, no reaggregation
else complete
 E --> W : publish complete file/count/sum/checksum
end
note over P,S
 recordedAt can precede physical commit/midnight crossing.
 A source contributes BASE OR ADJUSTMENT, never both.
 Retry after snapshot commit preserves source set even if aggregation failed.
 Failure before source freeze still preserves the original durable cutoff.
 Missing days recovered in order; no client-supplied backdating.
end note
@enduml
